  message: "WONT_DO — the named instance does not reproduce, and the general framing rests on a category error an existing ruling already settled.\n\nFiled: 'meta.framework_dispatch names fastapi/django_channels absent from profile.frameworks; two surfaces contradict.'\n\nMeasured on a fresh self-survey:\n  framework_dispatch values: registry_dispatch 296, npm_package 8, starlette 2, rust_trait_dispatch 1, native_websocket 1\n  profile.frameworks: [lit, protobuf, pytest, starlette]\n\n(1) Neither fastapi nor django_channels appears in framework_dispatch at all, so the specific contradiction filed is gone. (2) The one value that IS a framework name — starlette — appears in profile.frameworks too, so it agrees rather than contradicts.\n\n(3) The general reading is the category error. The remaining values (registry_dispatch, npm_package, rust_trait_dispatch, native_websocket) are dispatch MECHANISMS, not framework names, so their absence from profile.frameworks is correct rather than a disagreement. This is settled: INV-junid's four-lens ADR/spec/history/spirit review (register pt.19, PR #753) ruled framework_dispatch a coherent 'framework-dispatch CONVENTION' axis whose values are deliberately BOTH framework-specific compounds (django_orm, kafka_streams) AND framework-agnostic mechanisms (registry_dispatch, npm_package) — and explicitly declined promoting it to a typed Edge.framework. Treating it as a list of framework names, then diffing it against profile.frameworks, is the reading that review rejected.\n\nClosing wont_do rather than done: there is nothing to fix, and reopening would need a NEW instance where a genuine framework compound is missing from profile.frameworks."  # 06d9
